Package: PlaceboLM
Title: Causal Progress with Imperfect Placebos Using Linear Models
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Adam", "Rohde", , "adamrohde@ucla.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Partial identification of causal effects using imperfect placebo
    variables, implementing the omitted-variable-bias framework of Rohde and
    Hazlett. Given a placebo outcome or placebo treatment sharing unobserved
    confounders with the treatment-outcome relationship of interest, users
    postulate ranges for two sensitivity parameters -- relative confounding
    (either the raw bias ratio 'm' or its scale-free counterpart 'k') and the
    degree of placebo imperfection -- and obtain the corresponding range of
    defensible effect estimates. Conventional difference-in-differences is
    recovered as the point assumption m = 1, so the framework provides a
    reasoned relaxation of parallel trends. Supports five causal structures,
    bootstrap inference, bounds over assumption ranges, tipping-point
    calculation, and contour and line visualisations.
